      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T17:07:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we just write a totally-random serial number into PreMP boards just before setting the PreMP flag?\n\nThen you could match against that on your test server.",
      "parentUuid": "27ce3396_28858687",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1446b8e4_436a21a1",
        "filename": "chip/g/sn_bits.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1161144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T19:08:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am sure we could, but we would also need the full SN to be in the VPD since INFO1 only has bits of a hash. So at that point we\u0027re basically asking the factory for a more complicated step, which may not be reasonable, rather than some in dev and test being able to write the SN and bits they want as needed.",
      "parentUuid": "d280ff2c_ff2fb56f",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
