    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b91b5c12_42f12938",
        "filename": "chip/g/sn_bits.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1161144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-19T01:07:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because they\u0027re the first ones out when we test other parts of Chrome OS etc.? The eve I use for development and testing for example are DVTs because that\u0027s what Chromestop sent me. Arbitrarily blocking those boards from being able to be used for a part of Chrome OS doesn\u0027t seem like a good idea. Just like preventing erasure of INFO1 would make your life quite difficult you said, preventing non-MP boards from doing core parts of the enterprise flows for Chrome OS would make testing and development much more difficult too.",
      "parentUuid": "71c54eb2_e018f5d2",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4891d659_6a4f26f6",
        "filename": "chip/g/sn_bits.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1161144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-19T01:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So it\u0027s not about requiring pre-MP boards for testing, it\u0027s about not excluding them from being able to do all the enterprise flows of Chrome OS in a test environment.",
      "parentUuid": "b91b5c12_42f12938",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c12e11df_9b5f76f9",
        "filename": "chip/g/sn_bits.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-22T03:11:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok so the goal is to reduce the number of early stage devices that are eligible for [production] ZTE, whilst still allowing an arbitrary SN to be written to those devices so they can be used for testing.\n\nThis requires changes in:\n- cr50 board ID code\n- cr50 SN bits code\n- factory tooling\n- board ID validation in asbestos? (to check for premp bit on otherwise valid field) \n- qa borgconfig for asbestos to ignore above validation\n\nThe plan all makes sense, but above is a fair bit of work, not to mention additional complexity and room for error.\n\nChromestop in Taipei at least has many PVT devices and obtaining one is never a problem - if there is any chance of doing this in your office, and there are no other reasons to test on DVT devices, then I\u0027d suggest we just skip doing the above. \n\nIf it\u0027s possible to test on a PVT device but is still important to reduce the number of early stage devices eligible for ZTE, perhaps we could do this by just writing the fixed \u0027premp\u0027 board id (ZZCR), which would presumably only need a change to factory tooling.",
      "parentUuid": "4891d659_6a4f26f6",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2957ea7_b82676f4",
        "filename": "chip/g/sn_bits.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-22T07:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, the real goal is to ship early stage devices in a state where they can\u0027t pretend to be a real device.  Writing the entire PreMP board ID would be sufficient.\n\nWhat if we change the code which writes the serial numbers so that it will allow writing if *either*:\n   1) BoardID has not yet been set\n   2) BoardID has been set to ZZCR / PreMP flags\n\nThen we can just blindly write the BoardID to ZZCR early in proto/EVT factory runs and leave the serial number field blank.  When devices arrive at Google, we can write whatever serial number we want for ZTE testing.  But since BoardID has already been written to ZZCR, they\u0027ll never match any real MP device.",
      "parentUuid": "c12e11df_9b5f76f9",
      "revId": "f6a39cb60456f911aed5745e79b2f39d833b616c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
